  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Hong shao rou is built on patience. The pork belly goes through three stages: blanching to remove impurities, an initial sear to colour the skin, then a long "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "red-braise"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "red braise"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " that slowly tenderises the meat and thickens the sauce."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "rock-sugar"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "rock sugar"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " if you can find it. It gives a deeper gloss than caster sugar. If not, light brown sugar works well."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
